   "text": {
    "L1": "Integers include counting numbers, zero, and their negatives.",
    "L2": "Negative numbers are real and useful, so the idea that they are not real is not true.",
    "L3": "Zero is a reference point. It can mean ground floor, 0 degrees Celsius, or owing nothing.",
    "L4": "We choose a positive direction, and a negative number shows the opposite direction.",
    "L5": "On this number line, numbers below zero are negative and numbers above zero are positive.",
    "L6": "A profit of 200 is +200, while a loss of 150 is −150.",
    "L7": "B2 is two floors below ground floor 0, so its integer is −2, not +2.",
    "L8": "Now check your understanding: choose the integer for B2."
   },
